// NEGATIVE TEST -- `pub` on a top-level item is not implemented (N3-09, N3-10).
//
// `pub` PROMISES A VISIBILITY NOTHING DELIVERS. The resolver does not export a
// `const` or a `static` (src/resolver/mod.rs), and code generation emits a
// definition only for the program being compiled -- so an importer that writes
// the name gets "Undefined variable or function" at the USE site: a diagnostic
// about the reader's spelling, for a decision the language made.
//
// Refused where the word is written. The item is visible to every function in
// its own file with or without it, so the repair is to delete four characters.
// Making `pub` mean something here is cross-module code generation, which is
// N11's work and not N3-09's.
pub const X: i64 = 1;

fn main() {
    print_int(X);
}
